From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Haapanen <ian.haapanen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:36:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] x86/knc: host memory for the card: /dev/phiblk1 over
 ring channel 5, /dev/phihost

The host tool pins a shared file for the card and announces its card
address and size in the ring region header (REGION_HOSTMEM_ADDR and
_SIZE); the card reaches it through the system memory page table at
0x80_0000_0000 and up (SSDG 328207-002, 2.1.12).

knc_blk.c becomes multi-instance: channel kind 4 is /dev/phiblk0 (the
disk image) and kind 5 /dev/phiblk1, backed by that host memory and
served by the DMA engine straight between the window and the card's
pages. A channel without bounce slots works in direct mode only. The
card's init runs mkswap and swapon on /dev/phiblk1 at every boot, which
extends the card's 6 GB by the size the host gives.

knc_hostmem.c adds /dev/phihost, root only: read, write, llseek (size at
the end) and mmap (uncached) of the same window, so a card program and a
host program share bytes with no copy. Every access is a PCIe
transaction; bulk traffic belongs on /dev/phiblk1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
